Purpose: QA observed that the stopped-schema assertions are all about what does
not happen, so an implementation refusing every Realm at the schema boundary
would satisfy them. This mutant is that implementation.

--- cargo test -p kontor-daemon --bin kontor-daemon -- a_realm_stopped_before_the_current_schema
test tests::a_realm_stopped_before_the_current_schema_refuses_without_reading_or_installing ... ok
test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 9 filtered out

    ^ exactly QA's point: the stopped-schema test cannot tell the difference.

--- cargo test -p kontor-daemon --bin kontor-daemon -- a_current_realm_reaches_the_credential_reader
thread 'tests::a_current_realm_reaches_the_credential_reader_and_fails_after_the_gate' panicked at
crates/kontor-daemon/src/main.rs:967:9:
a current realm did not reach the credential reader: Err(CredentialScope)
test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 9 filtered out

    ^ the hardened control catches it. That is what makes the pair evidence
      rather than a restatement.
